sion, let <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">T</span></code> be <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">decltype<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>e<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>, and let <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">U</span></code> be <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/remove_cvref\"><span class=\"kw2661\">std::<span class=\"me2\">remove_cvref_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code>. Then the expression <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">views<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">as_const</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>e<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> is <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/expressions#Expression-equivalence\">expression-equivalent</a> to:\n<ul><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/all_view\"><span class=\"kw2935\">views::<span class=\"me2\">all</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>e<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>, if it is a well-formed expression and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/all_view\"><span class=\"kw2934\">views::<span class=\"me2\">all_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code> models <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/constant_range\"><code>constant_range</code></a>;\n</li><li> otherwise, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/span\"><span class=\"kw2648\">std::<span class=\"me2\">span</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> X, Extent<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>e<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> for some type <code>X</code> and some extent <code>Extent</code> if <code>U</